@startuml
left to right direction

actor User

rectangle "Web Application (Auth System)" {
  User -- (Register with Email/Password)
  User -- (Login with Email/Password)
  User -- (Logout)
  User -- (Request Password Reset)
  User -- (Verify Email)
  User -- (Register/Login with Social Account)

  (Register with Email/Password) .> (Receive Registration Feedback) : include
  (Register with Email/Password) .> (Trigger Email Verification) : include

  (Login with Email/Password) .> (Receive Login Feedback) : include
  (Login with Email/Password) .> (Check Email Verification Status) : include

  (Request Password Reset) .> (Receive Password Reset Instructions) : include

  (Verify Email) .> (Confirm Account Ownership) : include
  (Verify Email) .> (Request New Verification Link) : extends

  ' Optional Account Management Use Cases
  User -- (Change Email Address)
  User -- (Delete Account)
}

' Notes based on user story details
note right of (Register with Email/Password)
  Clearly indicate if email exists
  or password is weak.
end note

note right of (Login with Email/Password)
  Receive clear feedback on
  incorrect credentials.
end note

note right of (Verify Email)
  Prompted after registration.
  Clear email instructions.
end note

note right of (Check Email Verification Status)
  Remind/Restrict unverified users
  until email is confirmed.
end note

note top of User
  Represents any user interacting
  with authentication features.
end note


@enduml